# NewBoard knowledge graph (MFCB_BASE)

Reference for OPS_ZF → NewBoard migration. **Headers only** in workspace for OPS (precompiled `libops.a`); behaviour lives in `.c` inside the library.

## Header sources (read this first)

| Label | Path | Role |
|-------|------|------|
| **CURRENT** | `NewBoard/MFCB_BASE/CM7/OPS_Lib/include/` (mirrored on CM4) | Matches **linked firmware today** (174 public `.h` files) |
| **NEWER** | `NewBoard/Newer_build_includes/include/` | **Incoming build** — not linked yet (205 `.h` files) |

When mapping OPS_ZF features, prefer **NEWER** APIs if they exist (SBUS, FDCAN task, crypto). Code against CURRENT until the new `libops.a` arrives.

## ⚠️ CRITICAL — check the OPS function inventory FIRST

**Before designing any workaround for OPS/libops behaviour, search
`.cursor/Logs/Log6-OPS-function-inventory.md`** — every public OPS function (832, CM4 vs CM7
availability marked, briefs included, cross-checked against both `libops.a` binaries).
The library almost certainly already has the function you need.
Proven example: a full day lost working around the OPS UART RX task stealing UART6 for SBUS —
the fix was the pre-existing `UART_Task_StopPort(6)`. The inventory also lists customer-overridable
hooks (e.g. `UART_Task_OnFrame`) and lib-internal symbols you must not collide with
(e.g. `HAL_UART_RxCpltCallback` is already defined inside CM4 libops.a).

