## Dual-core rule (mandatory)

- **CM4 owns** real-time HAL: UART, I2C, ADC, PWM, FDCAN, SPI2/4, DAC chip, EEPROM, RS-485.
- **CM7 owns** LwIP, web server, USB, SD, QSPI, KSZ9897 (SPI5), crypto accelerators.
- **Callers use one API on both cores** — module `.c` picks HAL vs ICC (`adc_read_raw`, `DAC_OutputVoltage`, `pwm_in_ctrl`, `I2C_ReadByte`, …).
- **Never** `#if CORE_CM4` around peripheral calls in Customer code.
- **ICC** (`peripherals/inter_core_communication/intercore_comm.h`): SRAM4 rings, `ic_channel_t` per bus (`IC_CH_ADC`, `IC_CH_PWM`, `IC_CH_NETWORK`, `IC_CH_CUSTOMER`, …).

