## UART1 / UART6 / UART7 allocation (CURRENT porting, 2026-07-06)

Full bench log: `.cursor/Logs/Log2-SBUS-config-path-NewBoard.md`.

| Port | Role | Voltage |
|------|------|---------|
| **UART1** | **Debug** — CM4 + CM7 (`CM4/CM7_INIT_DEBUG_UART`, Customer UART) | 3.3 V @ 115200 (no `UART_SetVoltage` API) |
| **UART6** | **SBUS RC RX** — OPS_ZF / NEWER inst1 | 3.3 V now → **`SUPPLY_VOLTAGE_5V`** + `UART_SetVoltage(&huart6, …)` when needed |
| **UART7** | **SBUS TX mirror** | 3.3 V now → **`SUPPLY_VOLTAGE_5V`** + `UART_SetVoltage(&huart7, …)` when needed |

Override supplier defaults (debug was UART7 CM4 / UART6 CM7). **5 V:** change `RC_SBUS_RX_VOLTAGE` / `RC_SBUS_TX_VOLTAGE` in `rc_sbus_config.h` + matching `UART_SetVoltage` calls — **UART6/7 only**.

**HAL:** CM4 owns UART HAL. SBUS init in CM4 Customer only; CM7 debug on UART1 goes ICC → CM4.

**CURRENT SBUS:** Hardcode `uart_config_t` + Phase 2 explicit **100000 Hz**; web lacks 100k baud.

**Debug probe:** One cable on **UART1** @ 115200; flash both cores.

